{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation","id":452497,"title":"Harmony Observation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T04:41:22-07:00","id":452497,"title":"Harmony Observation","content":"I've been enjoying testing the new Werewolf 2.0 rules. I noticed during play that it seems to be easier to Break Toward Flesh (BTF) than to Break Towards Spirit (BTS). I have no strong feelings about this, but I am curious if this was the design intent.<ul><li>A Werewolf wanting to BTF could easily mate with a human (slight social consequences), eat processed food (no consequences), or allow a friendly spirit or totem into the physical world to hang out for a bit (??? consequences).</li> <li>A Werewolf wanting to BTS could kill a wolf or human (moderate social consequences), stay away from his pack (in game and out of game consequences), or take vacations in the Hisil (dietary, spiritual, or out of game consequences).</li> </ul>The only easy option on the list is lead a Siskur-Dah, which means other members of the pack who also need to BTS <b>are not leading it</b>, but must still participate or they BTF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 03-22-2015, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T05:36:43-07:00","id":452540,"title":"","content":"I started a search for all the breaking points listed in the book (assuming that not all of them would be on that handy chart on page 104). I got as far as that chart before finding something for you.<br /> With the exception of killing a wolf or human, everything you listed is from the above 8 harmony or below 3 harmony lists. The formatting is messed up, and I posted as such to the errata threads, but the last few on each list are breaking points towards that are easier to hit when you're way out of balance.<br /> Were they not in place, then the only mechanic affecting how fast you slide one direction or the other would be the penalty to your roll for how far out you are (described in the text on that page). It makes it harder to resist BingTF when you're above 5 and harder to resist BingTS when you're below 5, though, so that would mean all mechanics are a slippery slope away form true harmony.<br /> Most of those points you listed are the counterbalance towards that to allow you to keep yourself in check if you're halfway down that slope in either direction. The ones that count out of the gate (7 Harmony) are (and my appologies if this is pulling too much from the book at once):<br /> TOWARD FLESH<br /> \u2022 Defiling a locus.<br /> \u2022 Refusing to participate in Siskur-Dah.<br /> \u2022 Staying out of the Hisil for a week.<br /> \u2022 Using a silver weapon against another werewolf. <br /> \u2022 Violating the Oath of the Moon. (-2)<br /> \u2022 Staying out of the Hisil for a month. (-3)<br /> TOWARD SPIRIT<br /> \u2022 Killing a human or wolf.<br /> \u2022 Staying in the Hisil for a week.<br /> \u2022 Hunting humans or wolves for food (\u20132)<br /> \u2022 Killing a packmate. (\u20132)<br /> \u2022 Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence (\u20133)<br /> \u2022 Staying in the Hisil for a month. (-3)<br /> <br /> Leading a Siskur-Dah won't affect your Harmony unless the first breaking point you fail was for using silver or violating the oath of the moon (which would be easy to fail as it would be at a cumulative -4 between its nature and the already out of harmony penalty). That said, killing humans looks to always be a towards spirit breaking point. They tend to end up being collateral damage in a lot of hunts, even if they're not the prey. As such, that should be a good place to start with heading towards true Harmony.<br /> <br /> One last comment: Harmony is supposed to be the stat that reminds you that you are playing a monster. Breaking points towards spirit are about indulging that monster and breaking points towards flesh are about pretending that you're not a monster. They're supposed to be a big deal, even though you need to break them to keep yourself together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 03-22-2015, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T05:47:53-07:00","id":452545,"title":"","content":"If you want your people breaking towards spirit quickly, here's a thought that will also add a fair amount of drama:<br /> Have a handful of the periphery human packmates do something treacherous for which they need to be hunted down. Then your wolves will be at a -2 to their roll and they'll have to wonder about the general integrity of their pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T05:49:52-07:00","id":452548,"title":"","content":"You know, I was white-rooming Harmony rolls, beginning at Harmony 7 and alternating rolls between flesh and spirit with adjusted modifiers for the Anchored merit towards spirit, and yeah even then after a dozen rolls it always ended up towards Harmony 9 or 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:18:33-07:00","id":452586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452540#post452540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started a search for all the breaking points listed in the book (assuming that not all of them would be on that handy chart on page 104). I got as far as that chart before finding something for you.<br /> With the exception of killing a wolf or human, everything you listed is from the above 8 harmony or below 3 harmony lists. The formatting is messed up, and I posted as such to the errata threads, but the last few on each list are breaking points towards that are easier to hit when you're way out of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I had not even considered that the formatting might be messed up. The way I was reading the chart, reaching Harmony 8 or more / Harmony 3 or less was a breaking point in the other direction (giving you one chance to swing back each time you hit an extreme harmony level). Essentially a way to stabilize the descent / ascent to either extreme.<br /> <br /> That does take a lot of the really easy BTF off the table.<br /> Though the BTS options still seem have considerably more consequences than the BTF options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:44:05-07:00","id":452616,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it has to be a formatting error. Otherwise, a day and a week in or out of the Hisil is a breaking point of the same severity. Also, it makes sense that when you're way out of line the easier things come on the table. By that point you're so far inhuman/unspirit that your other side would accept any shred of ascent.<br /> <br /> As to social consequences, it makes sense that the BTS ones would seem more severe. You're a werewolf living in a world of humans and puppeted by a human (player), so acting more human would have fewer consequences than acting like a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:52:45-07:00","id":452687,"title":"","content":"I remember in the dev blog on Harmony, it was said that a lot of things Werewolves just do all the time as part of being werewolves would break them towards spirit, and that a gradual slide towards lower Harmony would be the default unless you actively took measures to preserve your human side. I liked that idea a lot, but the sample breaking points seem to kind of do the opposite. That said, there are other hard-coded breaking points elsewhere in the book. For example, eating a spirit's essence on the Siskur-Dah is a BTS, one which I imagine will happen quite often for most packs. And the listed breaking points are only examples, the ST can always call for a breaking point when it feels appropriate, even if it's not one of the examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:04:21-07:00","id":452746,"title":"","content":"Using Influences may be a breaking point towards spirit, using certain facets may be a breaking point towards spirit (like the Honor facet from Change. You became more like an spirit, so it could push you to that side), changing shape several times in a row may be too, there are plenty of options besides those explicitely stated in the book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:07:40-07:00","id":452861,"title":"","content":"Cannibalism is both an affront to the Oath and a spiritual breaking point... how do we handle those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:12:53-07:00","id":452869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452861#post452861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cannibalism is both an affront to the Oath and a spiritual breaking point... how do we handle those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either roll them both or have the ST decide which seems like the bigger breach. For the former, I'd probably have the ST decide which would go first and not roll the second one if the first one failed.<br /> Or maybe that was somehow an oversight that will be revised after the errata are fixed and we'll get a more solid answer soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:13:07-07:00","id":452870,"title":"","content":"I don't think every mandate in the oath need be a Breaking Point towards Flesh. The oath is a social contract, not a list of things that will make you less spirit-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:25:20-07:00","id":452922,"title":"","content":"I'd say specific trumps general. Breaking the oath is towards flesh except when it's also a breaking point the other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:31:23-07:00","id":452938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452870#post452870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think every mandate in the oath need be a Breaking Point towards Flesh. The oath is a social contract, not a list of things that will make you less spirit-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, thought? It's the Oath of the Moon for supernatural People for whom the Moon is a supernatural parent figure. It seems like it would have actual weight beyond just being a social contract.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm thinking that I would take an act of cannibalism wherein your intention from the start was to hunt the person/wolf down for food would be a break towards spirit. That's premeditated action as only spirits would take. Eating your Agg-Flakes in the heat of battle to grab power while actually causing harm to an otherwise unkillable enemy, though, would could as more of a breach of the oath, and thus be a break towards flesh.<br /> So in practice I guess I agree with Charlaquin, but I find questioning the nature of the Oath of the Moon interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:58:55-07:00","id":452965,"title":"","content":"For cannibalism, I'd pick whichever side they were closest to on the principle that I refuse to reward it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:03:46-07:00","id":452971,"title":"","content":"I would make it be a breaking point toward Spirit every time. The consequences outside of Harmony loss are bad enough as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:06:12-07:00","id":452973,"title":"","content":"Doing nasty shit and getting away with it is an entirely sustainable life model in the WoD if you can pull it off. That's one of the reasons the place is such a basket of crap for normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:09:13-07:00","id":452979,"title":"","content":"After having gone further with my seach of the phrase &quot;breaking point toward&quot; in the PDF, I found that using the Siskur-Dah to hunt down a spirit that can give you the opening Facet of a new Gift counts as BTS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:20:04-07:00","id":452992,"title":"","content":"That's only if it gives you a gift and then you rudely decide to eat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:36:13-07:00","id":453017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452938#post452938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it, thought? It's the Oath of the Moon for supernatural People for whom the Moon is a supernatural parent figure. It seems like it would have actual weight beyond just being a social contract.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm thinking that I would take an act of cannibalism wherein your intention from the start was to hunt the person/wolf down for food would be a break towards spirit. That's premeditated action as only spirits would take. Eating your Agg-Flakes in the heat of battle to grab power while actually causing harm to an otherwise unkillable enemy, though, would could as more of a breach of the oath, and thus be a break towards flesh.<br /> So in practice I guess I agree with Charlaquin, but I find questioning the nature of the Oath of the Moon interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't mean to say it doesn't carry more spiritual weight than just a social taboo. I just don't think every violation of the oath should necessarily make you more human. Cannibalism is anathema to most humans, but a part of everyday life for spirits, so it doesn't make sense that doing it would ever make a werewolf more human. There are other ways to punish breach of supernatural contract than just Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:44:36-07:00","id":453024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452992#post452992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only if it gives you a gift and then you rudely decide to eat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, receiving the Gift does involve the bugger physically carving you up. Gotta be tempting to have a bite of Essence after the thing has been stabbing its talons in your guts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:00:17-07:00","id":454206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=452992#post452992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only if it gives you a gift and then you rudely decide to eat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about that. I missed the &quot;if they then bring the spirit down&quot; bit of it on my other read. It was nice of the writers to take away player incentive to be so rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:09:31-07:00","id":454444,"title":"","content":"Won't stop some players...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:28:26-07:00","id":454470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=454206#post454206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was nice of the writers to take away player incentive to be so rude.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be a matter of survival more than politeness when you're low on essence and in the Hisil, possibly far from a friendly locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:53:16-07:00","id":454508,"title":"","content":"In that case you shouldn't have gotten a gift, because once you've done that you don't get any essence from eating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:04:34-07:00","id":454523,"title":"","content":"Glory for one, Wisdom for another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:12:39-07:00","id":454538,"title":"","content":"I don't know that it's Glorious to kill a thing you just struck a deal with as soon as the exchange was made...<br /> Taking away all essence gains and making it a BTS point should probably deter most people that aren't smarting from an inflated Harmony rating...<br /> Then again, given how this thread started, that might be most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:21:44-07:00","id":454550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452497-harmony-observation?p=454538#post454538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that it's Glorious to kill a thing you just struck a deal with as soon as the exchange was made...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's right. I was wrong, I was originally thinking you could get the Essence even after getting the gift. But since you cannot, in the given situation your options are getting the gift, risking having low Essence in the Hisil, or getting your Essence and forsaking your gift. If the situation involves a rare find, in terms of gifts, the choice might be worth Renown, depending on the dangers involved.<br /> <br /> In my game my character's already eaten a human and is still at 7 Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}